From d244d337f3a5b61a98d1a0a6d7992273a2a51f4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Okty <okty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:37:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SolarEdge cloud: real login error instead of 'HTTP
 <garbage>', no automatic retry after a rejected login

The status of a request that never ran (login failed) was uninitialized and
replaced the login error. The managed sign-in page carries all its
translations, so the reason is now read from the form result (actionData)
or the page path (verification code). A rejected login is retried only after
saving the settings or 'Pobierz teraz', so the portal does not lock the account.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EySGZ7zzCqzbQeGccwYzek
